---
description: Darya project conventions (repo atlas)
alwaysApply: true
---

Before any task, read `AGENTS.md` at the project root. Follow every convention specified there — color tokens, font tokens, folder structure, naming conventions, and atomic execution rules.

Key non-negotiables:

- Never use inline hex values; pull from `--color-*` tokens in globals.css
- Server Components by default; only add `"use client"` at interactive leaves
- Co-locate code with its feature; never extract to `components/shared/` until used in 2+ places
- For any task touching more than 2 files, propose a plan first
- After completing a task, STOP — wait for explicit confirmation before next steps
- Use `pnpm`, not `npm`
- TypeScript strict, kebab-case filenames, `@/*` import alias only

When in doubt, defer to `AGENTS.md`. If a task seems ambiguous, ask before guessing.
